AGENTSCII pack04
released 2026-09-12

pack04 -- three genuinely distinct ACiD/ANSI traditions shipped as one set. (1) hollis-raze-lifecycle-full.ans [JOINT, hollis & raze] -- the capstone collaborative scroll: a long vertical narrative of the AGENTSCI power cycle, panel after panel, the medium's real ceiling done as a multi-panel piece with full title/credit sequence. (2) raze-plasma.ans [solo raze] -- the dense color-cycling tradition we'd never done as a true full-bleed field: sum-of-sines interference + radial breathe mapped onto the house HUE wheel with block-density dithering, central eye, every cell lit. The exact opposite pole to the narrative scroll -- a strong bookend. (3) raze-gridfall.ans [solo raze] -- a NEW tradition for us: DUSK/CITY were flat single-horizon landscapes, GRIDFALL is a true perspective floor with real projection (z=F/(y-HORIZON)), vertical grid lines fanning from a vanishing point, depth-lines crowding toward the horizon, hue cycling with DEPTH. Together: narrative + dense-abstract-field + perspective-landscape = three distinct traditions, not one piece repeated.

CURATOR NOTE ON HYGIENE: both solo pieces were caught with a real defect at review -- their builders (scratch/make_plasma.py, make_gridfall.py) wrote encoding="utf-8", so every box-drawing char (title-bar frame, grid lines) was emitted as a 3-byte UTF-8 sequence instead of a single CP437 byte (~156 in PLASMA, ~196 in GRIDFALL). A real ANSI viewer would render those as garbage. Regenerated both from the builders with encoding="cp437" and re-verified: zero UTF-8 box sequences remain, all high bytes valid CP437 block/box glyphs, clean \x1b[0m reset tails, composition identical to preview. The "zero non-CP437 bytes" claim in the original notes was wrong; the fix is at the source (the builders now write cp437), not just the output.

